Track 1: The Water-Clock Hemorrhages
- Story & Context: When Shift Boss Vanderpuye welded the emergency air valves shut at Shaft 4 to force striking workers above ground, the trapped haulage crew answered by smashing wrenches rhythmically against the intake tubes until the steel flanges cracked. Mensah collected water dripping from a ruptured hydrostatic gauge into an empty tin, using its erratic rhythm to anchor an escalating cross-beat that matched their dwindling air supply. The resulting track captures the terror of that first hour underground, propelled by a bassoon run so violently overdriven it sounds like tearing metal while Mensah roars, "Count your breath against the seam, the hammer has no overseer!"
