Track 2: Kofi’s Stolen Shift-Log
- Story & Context: Deep in the Tarkwa sump station, shift-clerk Kofi Mensah used a stub of charcoal to overwrite five years of falsified safety ledgers onto his denim overalls, documenting how seventy men were logged as missing rather than buried. As the air became thick with sulfur and wet slate dust, he read the dates and skipped shifts aloud over Ama’s low, churning contrabassoon ostinato, turning bureaucratic negligence into a frantic, weaponized confession. The rhythm intensifies around the sound of iron wrenches clanking against ventilation baffles as Kofi bellows his frantic admission, "I crossed out your hours to give the company their dawn!"
