Track 3: Whose Calendar Survives the Shaft?
- Story & Context: Recorded in the aftermath of the barricade being breached by company police, the group fled through an abandoned horizontal drift into an old ventilation chimney, hauling their instruments up maintenance ladders while sirens wailed two miles above. In the chimney's resonant updraft, Osei played blindingly fast, joyful highlife guitar figures through a dying battery-powered amplifier, defying the toxic fumes while the bassoon held a defiant, horn-like drone. The track dissolves into an unhinged communal chant where workers cast off surface measurements of time, shouting into the upward exhaust, "Your thirty-day month cannot cross this cage!"
